them the source of the version you run; set `source_code_url` in config.json if
you publish a modified copy elsewhere. The app links to it from Settings.

Changes made in this fork (2026, by PeytonG; see the git history for detail):
- Renamed the app to Meadhall, with new artwork, a pixel-art look, a bright purple
  default theme and a pixel color wheel for choosing the theme color.
- Voice channels use MatrixRTC so they interoperate with Element Call, including
  end-to-end encrypted media; heorot-voice-relay is kept as a fallback.
- Voice channels let members join calls (call membership power level); the
  Discord import no longer breaks power levels for restricted channels.
- Desktop: auto-updates from GitHub Releases, tray icon, open at login, and a
  permission handler restricting renderer permissions to the app.
- Typecheck fix, and unit, smoke, Synapse integration and Playwright E2E tests
  with GitHub Actions CI.
- Release builds (Windows, Linux, Android), security scanning and documentation.

